WEBVTT

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:03.020
Yujin, let's...

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:05.190
get married.

00:01:56.670 --> 00:01:58.300
Bring me some more adjusting pads!

00:01:57.890 --> 00:01:58.830
Hurry it up!

00:01:58.300 --> 00:01:59.340
We're running out of time, hurry!

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:00.620
Yes, coming.

00:02:01.450 --> 00:02:04.010
What are you doing, you're supposed to be right here.

00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:06.210
Can you bring me two of those?

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:07.370
Yeah, just bring it here.

00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:09.350
Could you all hurry up?

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:07.870
Congratulations!

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:12.170
You stand up too!

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:14.750
Congratulations!

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:15.920
Congratulations!

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:16.960
Thanks.

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:29.930
So you're just going to do it without my permission?

00:03:30.230 --> 00:03:31.390
<i>I'm sorry.</i>

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:33.290
Haven't I told you enough times?

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:36.570
Even if I let you guys do this, Ms. Mi Hee will never allow it!

00:03:36.690 --> 00:03:39.530
<i>I didn't call to ask for your permission.</i>

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:42.150
<i>I just want you to understand.</i>

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:46.580
<i>I want you to be on my side, just as you've always been. {on my side as in a supporter/friend, not physically on someone's side}</i>

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:48.540
<i>Mom, please...</i>

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:04.760
Why are you here?

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:06.930
I told you I'd give you a bouquet at the finale, didn't I?

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:10.180
So you at least upheld your promise, huh?

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:14.020
I feel like I've done you many wrongs.

00:04:18.770 --> 00:04:20.070
So what?

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:20.980
You're sorry?

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:23.070
Yeah, I am.

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:25.530
Then come back to me.

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:27.160
Chelin...

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:29.990
Just come back to me if you're sorry.

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:32.160
You know I can't do that.

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:34.740
Then why did you come?

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:36.250
Did Yujin tell you to?

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:38.750
Did she tell you to come and sympathize with me?

00:04:41.170 --> 00:04:42.460
I have a favor to ask.

00:04:43.590 --> 00:04:46.470
Yujin and I are getting married.

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:54.770
I'm sorry.

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:57.520
I just didn't know who else to turn to.

00:04:57.770 --> 00:05:02.070
I guess our children marrying each other just wasn't meant to be.

00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:07.530
But Yujin's still like a daughter to me;

00:05:07.950 --> 00:05:12.540
what did you mean when you said that something bad's happened to her?

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:14.580
Please tell me. {i was tempted to put "Pray, tell."}

00:05:15.910 --> 00:05:19.080
Ms. Mi Hee came and visited me.

00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:22.550
Why did Mi Hee...

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:25.090
It looks like her son and Yujin...

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:29.090
are in a relationship. {the reason for "in a relationship" over the tried and true "going out" here is because i don't think old people quite use that phrase the same way as we do... do correct me if i'm wrong, though.}

00:05:29.470 --> 00:05:31.430
Do you mean Joonsang?

00:05:32.390 --> 00:05:35.560
Did you know about this already, Mr. Kim?

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:41.440
So Joonsang and Yujin are really in a relationship?

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:44.940
What did Mi Hee have to say about it?

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:50.070
She asked me to stop them and oppose their relationship.

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:52.680
I don't know what's gotten into her;

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:53.950
she's not usually like this.

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:57.210
And now she's saying that they're getting married...

00:05:57.370 --> 00:05:58.460
Married?

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:14.930
So, you want us to congratulate you on getting married or something?

00:06:17.430 --> 00:06:18.770
Come on, Yongguk.

00:06:18.890 --> 00:06:20.770
I'll admit that it would have been okay if you just came to <i>us</i> about it,

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:25.400
but you're asking <i>Chelin</i> and even <i>Sanghyuk</i> to do the same?

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:28.150
You guys are all good friends of Yujin's.

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:35.120
You really are a piece of work.

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:36.540
You come back to life,

00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:38.200
you regain your memories,

00:06:38.200 --> 00:06:39.290
and now you're getting married to Yujin...

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:41.290
You're right;

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:43.400
it's certainly worthy of congratulations and celebration,

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:45.630
but do you have any idea how much pain this is causing everyone?

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:48.210
Yes, I'm sure Yujin suffered the most out of this whole ordeal,

00:06:48.470 --> 00:06:49.340
but it was hard for Sanghyuk,

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:50.340
for Chelin,

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:52.090
and all of us here!

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:54.510
We'd lived for over ten years,

00:06:54.510 --> 00:06:57.970
carefully trying to avoid letting the name "Joonsang" pass our lips!

00:06:58.930 --> 00:07:01.520
I'm not asking you to understand my position here,

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:04.480
but can't you see that something's wrong in all of this?

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:08.650
Why aren't we comfortably smiling and celebrating the fact

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:12.780
that two of our close friends like each other and are getting married?

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:13.370
Why?

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:14.660
Tell me!

00:07:15.330 --> 00:07:17.120
That's enough, Yongguk.

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:18.880
It's all your fault!

00:07:18.880 --> 00:07:20.330
I mean you haven't done anything wrong per se,

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:23.080
but it's all your fault!

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:25.000
Change it back!

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:26.540
Change everything back to before you died!

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:27.400
Yongguk...

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:31.130
Change everything back to before you came back to life again!

00:07:39.350 --> 00:07:40.930
Stop crying, will you!

00:07:41.060 --> 00:07:41.890
Chelin!

00:08:14.730 --> 00:08:15.390
Chelin!

00:08:15.540 --> 00:08:16.260
Let go!

00:08:17.350 --> 00:08:17.930
Watch out!

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:42.000
You better not be late today, Captain Tardy.

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:43.910
Don't you dare skip out today, you hear?

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:51.130
"In summation, her first fashion show was lost somewhere in the gray area

00:08:51.250 --> 00:08:56.090
between 'contemporary' and 'innovative' trends."

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:00.720
It was "lost," you say?

00:09:03.070 --> 00:09:04.660
Why isn't the store cleaned up yet?

00:09:05.180 --> 00:09:06.270
Hurry up with it!

00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:08.100
You're dead wrong,

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:10.440
if you think things are going to be more relaxed now that the show's over.

00:09:11.650 --> 00:09:13.280
What are you going to do about today?

00:09:13.650 --> 00:09:15.650
Are you going or not?

00:09:16.110 --> 00:09:18.410
Give me a clear answer so I can—

00:09:18.580 --> 00:09:19.340
<i>What about you?</i>

00:09:19.340 --> 00:09:20.450
<i>Are </i>you<i> going?</i>

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:21.580
<i>What did Chelin say about it?</i>

00:09:22.360 --> 00:09:23.250
<i>Hello?</i>

00:09:23.240 --> 00:09:24.950
<i>Jinsook?</i>

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:29.630
I-I really didn't want to go, but Yongguk kept...

00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:31.210
Go.

00:09:35.210 --> 00:09:36.720
Go before I change my mind.

00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:39.300
And take Yujin's dress from the upstairs atelier while you're at it.

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:42.480
What did I tell you about the hems?

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:43.680
Can't you do it right?

00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:49.730
You wouldn't happen to have anything that'd calm me down, would you?

00:09:50.350 --> 00:09:51.150
What for?

00:09:51.330 --> 00:09:52.330
I'm literally shaking

00:09:52.330 --> 00:09:54.150
at the thought of Mi Hee Kang actually coming here in the flesh.

00:09:54.330 --> 00:09:55.300
Why?

00:09:55.300 --> 00:09:57.110
You already saw her once at the concert, didn't you?

00:09:57.240 --> 00:09:59.660
It's not like it was up close and personal that time.

00:10:00.490 --> 00:10:03.660
We'll be alone all day today for the interview.

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:06.660
So you really did used to like her, then?

00:10:07.370 --> 00:10:09.500
Did you think I was joking?

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:11.170
Your first love lasts forever, you know.

00:10:12.340 --> 00:10:13.920
Oh man.

00:10:17.340 --> 00:10:18.380
Yes, Father?

00:10:19.510 --> 00:10:21.970
Why are you at the broadcasting station?

00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:24.720
We're here.

00:10:32.900 --> 00:10:34.440
What did you say?

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:38.490
Joonsang and Yujin are what?

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:40.490
Tell me, Father!

00:10:43.990 --> 00:10:44.870
Father!

00:10:46.350 --> 00:10:49.000
Joonsang is Hyeonsoo's son.

00:10:50.330 --> 00:10:52.960
Joonsang and Yujin are siblings.

00:10:56.000 --> 00:10:57.050
We have to stop them.

00:10:57.050 --> 00:10:59.470
We can't let them get married.

00:11:10.570 --> 00:11:11.560
Mi Hee.

00:11:33.580 --> 00:11:36.420
I never would have imagined that you'd find out as well.

00:11:36.840 --> 00:11:39.590
It was bound to happen one way or another.

00:11:40.010 --> 00:11:42.590
I heard Joonsang came to you.

00:11:44.010 --> 00:11:47.600
Does he know that Hyeonsoo is his father too?

00:11:50.600 --> 00:11:54.600
Do you remember what happened the night Hyeonsoo got married?

00:11:56.650 --> 00:11:59.730
After that happened, you left this place as if you were running away.

00:11:59.860 --> 00:12:03.400
Because of that, I thought Joonsang was my son this whole time.

00:12:04.030 --> 00:12:05.890
Why are you bringing up the past now?

00:12:05.890 --> 00:12:07.120
I don't want to hear any of it.

00:12:07.490 --> 00:12:10.120
So you were already with child back then.

00:12:10.790 --> 00:12:11.660
What do you mean?

00:12:12.250 --> 00:12:14.400
I thought you were merely

00:12:14.400 --> 00:12:16.920
infatuated with Hyeonsoo because he was "taken away" from you.

00:12:17.130 --> 00:12:18.630
But that wasn't it, was it?

00:12:19.670 --> 00:12:22.670
It was because you were already pregnant with Joonsang.

00:12:23.550 --> 00:12:24.470
So...

00:12:25.470 --> 00:12:27.400
Why didn't you tell Hyeonsoo?

00:12:27.400 --> 00:12:29.060
You wanted him for yourself, didn't you?

00:12:29.310 --> 00:12:31.300
Hyeonsoo probably wouldn't have left,

00:12:31.300 --> 00:12:33.640
if you had told him you were carrying Joonsang.

00:12:35.060 --> 00:12:37.360
Do you know what the difference between you and Hyeonsoo is?

00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:40.890
People in love tend to exhibit this quality

00:12:40.890 --> 00:12:43.400
where they unconditionally believe everything their partner says.

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:46.100
You loved me,

00:12:46.100 --> 00:12:48.660
but Hyeonsoo didn't.

00:13:29.700 --> 00:13:31.000
You look beautiful.

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:32.540
You really do.

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:36.160
Hold on a second, I brought the tiara too.

00:13:38.710 --> 00:13:40.170
I could have sworn I put it here;

00:13:41.290 --> 00:13:42.210
where did it go?

00:14:27.210 --> 00:14:29.260
<i>Forgive me, God.</i>

00:14:34.870 --> 00:14:37.060
Yujin Jung, please recite your vows.

00:14:37.470 --> 00:14:41.060
I, Yujin Jung, take you, Joonsang Kang, to be my husband.

00:14:41.560 --> 00:14:45.400
As God is my witness, I will love and honor you all the days of my life.

00:14:46.080 --> 00:14:49.150
Joonsang Kang, please recite your vows.

00:14:50.450 --> 00:14:52.450
I, Joonsang Kang,

00:14:53.490 --> 00:14:55.330
take you, Yujin Jung, to be my wife.

00:14:56.410 --> 00:14:59.870
I will love and honor you all the days of my life...

00:15:04.590 --> 00:15:06.090
all the days of my life...

00:15:07.210 --> 00:15:09.800
<i>Don't forgive me, God.</i>

00:15:12.820 --> 00:15:15.640
I, Joonsang Kang, take you, Yujin Jung, to be my wife.

00:15:15.890 --> 00:15:18.970
As God is my witness, I will love and honor you all the days of my life.

00:15:22.770 --> 00:15:23.810
Congratulations!

00:15:24.940 --> 00:15:26.320
Congratulations!

00:15:27.110 --> 00:15:28.070
Thanks.

00:15:32.030 --> 00:15:33.360
Sanghyuk...

00:15:35.700 --> 00:15:36.870
Sanghyuk...

00:15:39.370 --> 00:15:40.370
Hey, Sanghyuk.

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:45.670
Don't act like this, Sanghyuk.

00:15:46.880 --> 00:15:49.420
What are we going to do if something happens?

00:15:49.550 --> 00:15:51.970
He probably only came to congratulate them.

00:15:52.970 --> 00:15:54.840
Do something, will you?

00:15:56.760 --> 00:15:58.810
Come with me for a sec.

00:16:02.100 --> 00:16:03.690
Get on, Yujin.

00:16:08.480 --> 00:16:09.360
Come on, Sanghyuk!

00:16:09.550 --> 00:16:13.030
You said just yesterday that you'd let her go, didn't you?

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:17.160
You said you wanted her to be happy, didn't you?

00:16:17.620 --> 00:16:20.580
You held out so well until now.

00:16:20.870 --> 00:16:23.580
Why are you doing this all of a sudden?

00:16:24.000 --> 00:16:27.040
Do you guys trust me?

00:16:28.710 --> 00:16:30.100
Then don't ask.

00:16:30.100 --> 00:16:31.050
Just let me go.

00:16:49.860 --> 00:16:50.860
Are you all right?

00:16:53.440 --> 00:16:54.400
I'm sorry.

00:16:54.650 --> 00:16:56.070
I'm fine.

00:16:56.650 --> 00:17:00.370
I don't mind that we didn't get either Mom's or Sanghyuk's blessings.

00:17:02.410 --> 00:17:06.000
I'm okay with it, even if the whole world is against it.

00:17:06.080 --> 00:17:08.380
Stuff like that doesn't get me sad at all.

00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:12.420
I mean look how much I had to go through to meet you again.

00:17:15.590 --> 00:17:18.390
I'm never letting go of you ever again,

00:17:19.550 --> 00:17:20.890
so don't you let go either.

00:17:22.430 --> 00:17:24.270
You wanna go see the ocean?

00:17:26.870 --> 00:17:28.100
For our honeymoon.

00:17:28.580 --> 00:17:30.810
I need to make a quick stop before we go.

00:17:31.130 --> 00:17:31.900
Where?

00:17:33.110 --> 00:17:34.110
It's a secret.

00:17:56.470 --> 00:17:58.450
Make sure it comes out nice, okay?

00:17:58.720 --> 00:18:00.590
Well, of course!

00:18:00.840 --> 00:18:03.060
But since I've got such beautiful people as models,

00:18:03.180 --> 00:18:07.310
I wouldn't have to try too hard to make a masterpiece out of this.

00:18:07.480 --> 00:18:09.440
Don't worry about it.

00:18:10.020 --> 00:18:11.190
Let's see now.

00:18:11.440 --> 00:18:14.270
I like the way you two are sitting right now.

00:18:14.390 --> 00:18:16.320
Now hold still...

00:18:16.650 --> 00:18:18.990
Could you tilt your head a little to the left, young man?

00:18:19.110 --> 00:18:23.370
I know you're happy, but close your mouth a little, young man.

00:18:24.580 --> 00:18:27.310
I have to say, you two really look alike;

00:18:27.310 --> 00:18:29.580
you must love each other a lot.

00:18:29.920 --> 00:18:30.830
Do we?

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:33.040
Here I go, then!

00:18:46.350 --> 00:18:47.600
This is my first time at the ocean.

00:18:48.400 --> 00:18:51.100
You've seriously never been to the ocean before?

00:18:52.020 --> 00:18:54.520
No, this is my first time coming with <i>you</i>.

00:18:55.020 --> 00:18:58.150
So for us, this is our first ocean.

00:18:59.360 --> 00:19:00.570
You're right.

00:19:01.660 --> 00:19:03.370
Our first ocean.

00:19:05.160 --> 00:19:07.870
<i>And our last.</i>

00:19:27.970 --> 00:19:29.380
An impossible house?

00:19:29.380 --> 00:19:30.640
Yeah.

00:19:30.640 --> 00:19:34.860
Daddy always used to say that a loving heart is the best home that

00:19:34.980 --> 00:19:36.610
two loving people could have.

00:19:39.730 --> 00:19:42.170
I want to actually build a house that contains in it

00:19:42.170 --> 00:19:44.070
all the warmth of a loving heart.

00:19:44.990 --> 00:19:45.910
Sounds ridiculous, doesn't it?

00:19:46.580 --> 00:19:48.450
No, I want to help you do it.

00:19:48.990 --> 00:19:50.940
I've got quite a few sketches of it done,

00:19:50.940 --> 00:19:53.790
but I always get stuck when I actually try to design it.

00:19:54.420 --> 00:19:56.100
I'd like to take a stab at designing it too,

00:19:56.100 --> 00:19:58.090
if it'll really be the kind of house you say it'll be.

00:19:58.920 --> 00:20:00.260
It's a promise then!

00:20:00.380 --> 00:20:01.630
Wow, awesome!

00:20:01.880 --> 00:20:03.720
I want to live here.

00:20:13.640 --> 00:20:14.850
Tada!

00:20:30.790 --> 00:20:32.370
I found so many!

00:20:32.950 --> 00:20:34.080
You're rich now.

00:20:34.790 --> 00:20:37.970
Why do you think there're so many coins around here?

00:20:38.540 --> 00:20:41.630
They were probably dropped by the visitors who came last summer.

00:20:42.210 --> 00:20:44.420
I see.

00:20:45.440 --> 00:20:49.430
With this, I can buy 1, 2, 3 ice creams...

00:20:50.140 --> 00:20:51.770
No!

00:20:53.730 --> 00:20:55.400
The coins are in a summertime mood

00:20:55.400 --> 00:20:56.980
even though it's still winter here, aren't they?

00:20:58.480 --> 00:20:59.480
What should we do with this money?

00:21:00.410 --> 00:21:01.400
I don't know.

00:21:02.440 --> 00:21:05.030
Why don't we pick up a lot more of them and buy a boat like this one?

00:21:05.200 --> 00:21:06.030
A boat?

00:21:06.240 --> 00:21:07.490
That's right.

00:21:07.780 --> 00:21:11.550
Then we could just wander the seas together our whole life

00:21:11.550 --> 00:21:13.040
and never come back.

00:21:13.370 --> 00:21:16.040
But you'll have to come back some time.

00:21:17.330 --> 00:21:20.840
The boat will get rusty and old with time,

00:21:21.090 --> 00:21:23.170
and we'll get old too.

00:21:23.550 --> 00:21:27.090
And when that happens, we'll long to return.

00:21:28.340 --> 00:21:29.550
You're probably right.

00:21:31.300 --> 00:21:32.180
It won't work out, will it?

00:21:47.340 --> 00:21:48.150
Yujin.

00:22:10.840 --> 00:22:13.900
<i>You have reached the voicemail of Yujin Jung,</i>

00:22:13.900 --> 00:22:16.180
<i>please leave a message after the beep.</i>

00:22:29.950 --> 00:22:30.740
Hello?

00:22:31.740 --> 00:22:32.870
Where are you?

00:22:33.490 --> 00:22:34.770
Let's meet.

00:22:34.770 --> 00:22:35.790
Let's meet and talk.

00:22:39.210 --> 00:22:40.290
I'm counting on you.

00:22:46.710 --> 00:22:49.590
At least act a little surprised, will you?

00:22:49.880 --> 00:22:51.550
Were you calling someone?

00:22:52.260 --> 00:22:53.180
I was calling work.

00:22:53.430 --> 00:22:55.250
Where have you been?

00:22:59.060 --> 00:22:59.770
Tada!

00:23:00.440 --> 00:23:02.690
This is summer's gift to you.

00:23:05.940 --> 00:23:07.280
It wants you to remember winter.

00:23:12.110 --> 00:23:13.450
And this...

00:23:14.620 --> 00:23:16.280
is <i>my</i> gift to you.

00:23:24.500 --> 00:23:28.090
Now you can beat fate.

00:23:29.130 --> 00:23:30.510
Give it a try.

00:23:31.170 --> 00:23:32.970
Only good answers will be waiting for you.
